{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01274",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.27,
      "end_seconds": 6.31,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "Afternoon, doctor. They're in and comfortable, and I have the measurements ready."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.52,
      "end_seconds": 12.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "Thank you. Good morning, tell me what's been going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 14.25,
      "end_seconds": 18.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "Doctor, I'm just here to help with the details."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 20.2,
      "end_seconds": 26.9,
      "duration_seconds": 6.7,
      "text": "Okay, so I'm here because of a dry cough in the evenings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.16,
      "end_seconds": 31.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.95,
      "end_seconds": 35.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Around a week, I think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 36.03,
      "end_seconds": 39.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "It was closer to two weeks, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.68,
      "end_seconds": 47.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.66,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly one to two weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.34,
      "end_seconds": 49.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.01,
      "text": "Yeah, roughly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.88,
      "end_seconds": 58.07,
      "duration_seconds": 8.19,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.94,
      "end_seconds": 66.85,
      "duration_seconds": 6.91,
      "text": "A eight out of ten, I suppose. It's once or twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.74,
      "end_seconds": 75.28,
      "duration_seconds": 7.54,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 75.38,
      "end_seconds": 80.3,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.06,
      "end_seconds": 88.9,
      "duration_seconds": 7.84,
      "text": "I was getting to that! Oh, and itchy eyes. That's been about the same, about a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.14,
      "end_seconds": 94.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.99,
      "end_seconds": 100.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "Severe, really. It's worse with outdoors. It comes and goes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.84,
      "end_seconds": 104.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "What operations have you had, if any?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.97,
      "end_seconds": 110.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "I had a bunion operation six years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.64,
      "end_seconds": 114.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.06,
      "end_seconds": 132.89,
      "duration_seconds": 17.83,
      "text": "I've had heart disease, yes. Mm, I've had acid reflux, yes. It's the not knowing that gets to me. I took the morning off to come in today. Anxiety, for nearly five years. Yes, an underactive thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.29,
      "end_seconds": 145.96,
      "duration_seconds": 7.67,
      "text": "Right, so acid reflux and an underactive thyroid are already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.05,
      "end_seconds": 165.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.03,
      "end_seconds": 168.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "I've never touched a cigarette."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.07,
      "end_seconds": 171.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.28,
      "end_seconds": 180.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.11,
      "end_seconds": 183.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "Right, is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.62,
      "end_seconds": 192.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.83,
      "end_seconds": 195.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Tell me about your eating."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.4,
      "end_seconds": 202.4,
      "duration_seconds": 6.0,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.83,
      "end_seconds": 206.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Let's run through your medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.96,
      "end_seconds": 212.94,
      "duration_seconds": 5.98,
      "text": "I'm on aspirin, 75 milligrams, once a day for my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.32,
      "end_seconds": 214.3,
      "duration_seconds": 0.98,
      "text": "Hm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.9,
      "end_seconds": 230.94,
      "duration_seconds": 15.04,
      "text": "Thyroxine, 75 micrograms, every morning. Loratadine. I take it 10 milligrams, once a day. Okay, so I'd been on pantoprazole, not any more though, I stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.85,
      "end_seconds": 235.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.89,
      "end_seconds": 243.48,
      "duration_seconds": 5.59,
      "text": "Um, my uncle has high cholesterol. My father has Parkinson's disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.71,
      "end_seconds": 247.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.28,
      "end_seconds": 250.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "No allergies at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.56,
      "end_seconds": 254.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Did you get shortness of breath or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 255.92,
      "end_seconds": 266.73,
      "duration_seconds": 10.81,
      "text": "No, no shortness of breath, no fever. I did have sneezing fits at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.8,
      "end_seconds": 269.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "What about wheeze?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 270.13,
      "end_seconds": 271.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "Definitely no wheeze."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.84,
      "end_seconds": 276.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Anything on the skin I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.57,
      "end_seconds": 280.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "No, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.98,
      "end_seconds": 284.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Okay, anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 285.26,
      "end_seconds": 288.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "That's normal as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 305.88,
      "end_seconds": 317.64,
      "duration_seconds": 11.76,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Temperature is 36.8 degrees, pulse is 71 beats a minute, oxygen saturation is 97 percent, respiratory rate 17, blood pressure 120 over 81."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.72,
      "end_seconds": 319.42,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.92,
      "end_seconds": 325.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 327.29,
      "end_seconds": 328.21,
      "duration_seconds": 0.92,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.84,
      "end_seconds": 332.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 349.44,
      "end_seconds": 354.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "Your chest is clear and your nose looks a little swollen inside."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 355.34,
      "end_seconds": 356.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.08,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 359.34,
      "end_seconds": 372.54,
      "duration_seconds": 13.2,
      "text": "All finished, thank you. From what you've told me and what I found, it fits best with seasonal hay fever causing the cough. Early asthma is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 374.49,
      "end_seconds": 375.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 376.61,
      "end_seconds": 398.73,
      "duration_seconds": 22.12,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's seasonal hay fever causing the cough, and we'll watch how it goes. The treatment will be fluticasone nasal spray, 50 micrograms, once a day, for the season. That should help with hay fever. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 399.88,
      "end_seconds": 404.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "Can I collect it from my own pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 405.37,
      "end_seconds": 417.15,
      "duration_seconds": 11.78,
      "text": "Keep windows closed on high-pollen days and wash your hair at night. If you start wheezing, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 417.84,
      "end_seconds": 420.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Alright, uh, I follow."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 422.35,
      "end_seconds": 430.05,
      "duration_seconds": 7.7,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in a month. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 431.97,
      "end_seconds": 433.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "That's clear, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 435.3,
      "end_seconds": 437.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.86,
      "text": "Have a good day."
    }
  ]
}